            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is an expected behavior of `vim.notify` override done by 'mini.notify'.\n\nThe `vim.notify` shows notifications [with specific levels](https://neovim.io/doc/user/lua.html#vim.notify()), which are [DEBUG, ERROR, INFO, TRACE, WARN, OFF](https://neovim.io/doc/user/lua.html#vim.log.levels). The INFO level is default.\n\nTo differentiate these levels, 'mini.notify' by default [uses `DiagnosticXxx` highlight groups](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/doc/mini-notify.txt#L279-L286). The `MiniNotifyNormal` is used for pure `add()` call (try `:lua MiniNotify.add('Hello')`).\n\nTo adjust highlighting groups for different levels, manually set `vim.notify` after `require('mini.notify').setup()`. [Like this](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/doc/mini-notify.txt#L260).",
