        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@micampe, I still received the e-mail notification about (what I assume is) now deleted comment and would like to address some of its points in good faith.\n\nI did and do appreciate not low effort issues (which this is) about improving 'mini.nvim'. And I did mean the \"Thanks for the issue\" in the first comment.\n\nI also said that adding additional note might be reasonable. Probably should have added that I'll think about it (which was the initial meaning of it). And I did, which resulted in [adding this note](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/2fc05996755c572e7820a5b64c4ffb326933fdd0/doc/mini-notify.txt#L52-L53) yesterday in the temporary branch of very big help file rework (didn't want to deal with possible merge conflicts if added directly to `main`).\n\nThe comment about searching was me being genuinely curious about negative result of \"I searched the docs\" when for me it feels reasonable to search for `highlight` and traverse 7 (not 70 or 700) matches. Should have asked about how you searched to maybe take in mind how people search stuff when writing docs in the future.\n\nAnd I still feel that current documentation is pretty discoverable in this use case. The repro uses `vim.notify()` and docs [very close to the top](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/2fc05996755c572e7820a5b64c4ffb326933fdd0/doc/mini-notify.txt#L13) already link to `make_notify()` for users who want to adjust `vim.notify()` override.\n\nHope this clarifies things. ",
